    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.hues, mini.base16\n\n### Description\n\nHi echasnovski! Currently, the terminal colors are being set by the colorscheme generated using mini.hues in this line https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/b07157c51e52a1b004ec7959f9618e9bc24686d3/lua/mini/hues.lua#L1370 and there is no way to turn it off. Is it possible to add some kind of option to plugins table to toggle these.",
