    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I don't think having terminal colors being not defined is a good idea. As you can see from the link you provided, terminal colors are defined through regular Vimscript global variables, i.e. `vim.g`. Toggling them should be a matter of custom helper function. For example:\r\n- If at least one color is set, cache all current values and unset then (with `vim.g.terminal_color_x = nil`).\r\n- Otherwise restore from cache and clear cache.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
